<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal copper strikers, management to meet.</title>
<headline>Portugal copper strikers, management to meet.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of Somincor, the company that manages Portugal's Neves Corvo copper mine, will meet representatives of striking miners on Thursday morning, a senior company official told Reuters.</p>
<p>But Raul Araujo, personnel director at Neves Corvo, said he was doubtful any progress could be made in resolving a dispute that has halted production at the 107,000-tonne per year mine since Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks very difficult to reach any accord,&quot; he said. Araujo said no exact time had been set yet for the talks to start.</p>
</text>
